WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.840
The second muscle we condition is agility.

00:04.840 --> 00:10.960
No game plan, no matter how brilliant, survives first contact with reality.

00:10.960 --> 00:16.360
Your 90-day plan is a roadmap, not a rigid set of tracks.

00:16.360 --> 00:19.080
Agility isn't about having a perfect plan.

00:19.080 --> 00:26.680
It's about being masterful at adapting to the plan without losing sight of the destination.

00:26.680 --> 00:30.440
Think about a marketing team that launches a major campaign.

00:30.440 --> 00:34.180
The initial data comes back, it's a flop.

00:34.180 --> 00:39.000
An agile leader doesn't see failure, they see feedback.

00:39.000 --> 00:43.900
They notice an unexpected surge of interest from a different demographic on a different

00:43.900 --> 00:45.640
platform.

00:45.640 --> 00:48.960
Instead of sticking to the original plan, they pivot fast.

00:48.960 --> 00:55.340
They reallocate resources to capitalize on the surprise opportunity, turning a potential

00:55.340 --> 00:58.700
loss into a huge win.

00:58.700 --> 01:01.500
That is agility in action.

01:01.500 --> 01:07.340
The best way to build this kind of agility is to anticipate the need to pivot before

01:07.340 --> 01:09.420
it even happens.

01:09.420 --> 01:14.940
In your playbook, you'll find a drill called stress testing your goals.

01:14.940 --> 01:20.540
You'll look at your 90-day plan and ask, where is this most likely to break?

01:20.540 --> 01:22.220
What's the weakest link?

01:22.220 --> 01:28.580
Identifying potential points of failure ahead of time can pre-plan your pivots.

01:28.580 --> 01:32.540
It's like a pivot practicing in a simulator.

01:32.540 --> 01:37.060
When the real thing happens, they don't panic, they execute.

01:37.060 --> 01:41.140
This proactive agility is the hallmark of an athlete.

